Slide 12: Training 3 — Loss Imbalance Analysis
Root cause of minADE/minFDE slight regression:
At end of training 3:
	∙	prediction_loss = 4.15
	∙	reg_loss = 0.50
	∙	w_pred × prediction_loss = 1.0 × 4.15 = 4.15
	∙	w_reg × reg_loss = 1.0 × 0.50 = 0.50
	∙	Imbalance ratio: 8.3x
MSE naturally produces larger values than smooth L1:
	∙	smooth_l1(3m error) ≈ 2.5
	∙	mse(3m error) = 9.0 — 3.6x larger
Optimizer spent 8x more gradient signal on agent prediction than ego planning
Result: interaction decoder improved significantly, planning decoder slightly regressed
Solution for Training 4: w_pred=0.5 reduces imbalance to ~4x

Slide 13: Training 3 — Anchor Improvements
Fixed anchor padding (Option 4):
Before — repeated first center:
	∙	np.repeat(centers[:1], reps, axis=0)
	∙	Multiple identical anchors → same FOPE encoding → wasted mode capacity
	∙	Minority classes (16K-35K samples) had many duplicate anchors
After — perturbed padding:
	∙	centers[random_choice] + Gaussian_noise(std=1.0m)
	∙	All Ka anchors start at distinct positions
	∙	Gradient signal immediately differentiates duplicate anchors from step 1
Learnable anchors:
	∙	register_buffer → nn.Parameter
	∙	Anchors receive gradients through FOPE → reg_loss path
	∙	Learn to position themselves where decoder can best cover GT endpoints
	∙	Converge to optimal initialization positions by epoch 15-20

