Slide 15: Training 4 — Design Rationale
w_pred=0.5 rationale:
	∙	Training 3 showed 8x imbalance hurting planning metrics
	∙	0.5 reduces to ~4x — still emphasizes agent prediction but not at planning expense
	∙	Expected: recover minADE to 0.75-0.80, keep PredAvgFDE gains
Velocity conditioning rationale:
	∙	PredAvgADE averages error over all timesteps
	∙	Fast agents accumulate large displacement errors without speed context
	∙	agent_vel_proj gives decoder explicit speed information per agent
	∙	Expected: 0.05-0.10 PredAvgADE improvement
Distance weighting rationale:
	∙	Distant stationary agents inflate PredAvgADE with easy-to-predict but irrelevant errors
	∙	Close agents within 20m are interaction-critical
	∙	2x weight focuses learning where it matters for TTC and collision metrics
	∙	Expected: 0.05-0.08 PredAvgADE improvement
Smoothness rationale:
	∙	Paper’s comfort score 98.16 — highest of all planners
	∙	Explicit jerk supervision directly targets comfort metric
	∙	1.9% of reg_loss contribution — stable, not dominant

