Slide 18: Training 5 — Iterative Refinement Design
Current limitation — fixed anchors through all decoder layers:
	∙	Mode queries initialized from FOPE-encoded anchors at layer 0
	∙	All 4 decoder layers process from same starting position
	∙	Large displacement from anchor to GT endpoint must happen in feature space only
Training 5 — per-layer anchor refinement:
	∙	After each decoder layer i: delta = tanh(interim_loc_head_i(x)) × 5.0m
	∙	Current anchors updated: current_anchors = current_anchors + delta
	∙	Position re-encoded via interim_pos_enc(delta) added to x with weight 0.1
	∙	Each layer refines position progressively toward GT endpoint
	∙	Final layer decodes trajectory from already-refined position
Expected impact:
	∙	Modes converge to GT endpoints more precisely
	∙	minFDE improvement 0.15-0.25
	∙	Progress score improvement from better goal reaching

